WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:02.601
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy Award-winning

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:03.870
co-host of "CBS Mornings,"

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.873
host of the SiriusXM show
"Gayle King in the House,"

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:09.976
and the editor-at-large
of "Oprah Daily."

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:12.145
The winter issue
of "O Quarterly,"

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:14.781
which features this year's list
of Oprah's Favorite Things

00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:17.350
is on newsstands now and
available at OprahDaily.com.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.518
Please welcome back
to the show,

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:20.620
our friend
Gayle King, everybody!

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.923
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:42.307 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:42.307 --> 00:00:43.909
Welcome back to the show.

00:00:43.909 --> 00:00:45.445
-I'm so glad to be here!

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:48.281
-I'm so excited to talk
about Oprah's Favorite Things,

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:50.617
but I do want to ask about
a couple of big interviews.

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:52.118
And of course, you do
a lot of big interviews,

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:55.789
but a couple of music legends --
Jay-Z, Barbra Streisand.

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:57.757
-I know, Seth.
All in the same week.

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.259
-That's amazing.

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:00.260
-I'm thinking, you know, guys,
you have a job where you go,

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.427
"just pinch me."

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:02.729
I really had a week.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:05.564
And I did them both
in the same week in October,

00:01:05.564 --> 00:01:06.599
and they're both from Brooklyn.

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:08.034
What does that mean?
Brooklyn!

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:09.202
What does that mean?

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:10.636
[ Cheering ]

00:01:10.636 --> 00:01:11.938
-And Barbra Streisand,

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:15.041
not the easiest interview
to land or do.

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:17.010
-No, Barbra Streisand,
her new book is out now.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.378
The title is
"My Name Is Barbra."

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:20.713
And make sure you say
her name right.

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:22.548
It's not "Strei-sind,"
it's not "Streisan."

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:24.517
It's "Strei-sand,"
like beach on a sand.

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:26.585
She's very particular
about that.

00:01:26.585 --> 00:01:28.754
And she told us back in the day
that they wanted her

00:01:28.754 --> 00:01:30.023
to change her name to "Sydney."

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:31.357
She was thinking about "Sydney."

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:33.325
They thought Sydney
would be a stronger name.

00:01:33.325 --> 00:01:36.095
She said, "I cannot do that,
but I will change the spelling."

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:39.399
So it's "Bar-bra."
So she did do that.

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:40.733
-That's lovely.
-She's amazing.

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.401
Well, that's so cool
that you did that.

00:01:42.401 --> 00:01:44.704
-Her memoir is close
to a thousand pages.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:47.639
I know it's a long read,

00:01:47.639 --> 00:01:49.509
but it's a good read.

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:51.510
But she really does take you
through her life.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.813
And I was just so thrilled
that she said, you know,

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.748
everybody was like,
"Pick me, pick me, pick me."

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:57.983
And I really was,
"Pick me, pick me."

00:01:57.983 --> 00:01:59.986
And she said yes.
-That's really cool.

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:03.722
Jay-Z, too. Jay-Z.
Don't we love Jay Z?

00:02:03.722 --> 00:02:05.992
[ Applause ]
Yes, we do!

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:08.294
I adore this man.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:10.462
And it started because
the Brooklyn Library has,

00:02:10.462 --> 00:02:12.231
you can go see it now

00:02:12.231 --> 00:02:14.099
until December 4th,
his birthday.

00:02:14.099 --> 00:02:17.670
It's called "The Book of Hove,"

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:19.872
and it takes you through
his career from the time

00:02:19.872 --> 00:02:22.975
he was a teenager to where
he is now, a business mogul.

00:02:22.975 --> 00:02:25.578
And I asked him, you know,
"I would love to go

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.146
see the exhibit
and do a walk and talk.

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:28.181
He said, "That's a good idea."

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:30.382
I go, "No, with you."
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:30.382 --> 00:02:33.319
-"No, no, not by myself.
With you."

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:35.621
-Well, very smart.
You're a very good interviewer.

00:02:35.621 --> 00:02:38.690
-No, I'm finding, Seth,
groveling really, really,

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:39.692
can be very effective.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:40.759
I'm not kidding.

00:02:40.759 --> 00:02:42.494
Oprah said to me,
"Stop asking him, Gayle.

00:02:42.494 --> 00:02:45.464
He doesn't want to do it.
You're embarrassing yourself."

00:02:45.464 --> 00:02:47.800
But I just thought
it was such -- number one,

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.235
and he rarely does interviews.

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.704
He's one of those
rare people like Taylor,

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.272
Bruce Springsteen, Beyonce.

00:02:53.272 --> 00:02:55.140
They don't have to do anything,
because we're all coming.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.842
-Yes.
-It's true.

00:02:56.842 --> 00:02:59.178
They don't have to do anything.
We're coming.

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:01.480
But if there ever was a time
to do the interview,

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.615
I guess his team convinced him.
I don't know.

00:03:03.615 --> 00:03:05.852
I'm just grateful
that he did it.

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.953
But to get to see
from his own words

00:03:07.953 --> 00:03:10.055
what he was thinking
when different songs came out

00:03:10.055 --> 00:03:11.257
and his writing process.

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:13.526
And you know,
where Blue got her name.

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:16.062
And he was really lovely.
Really, really.

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:17.730
-I'm going to ask him
to do my podcast.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.431
-Yeah.

00:03:19.431 --> 00:03:22.201
-No, no, no, I mean, we had
so much stuff on the floor.

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:24.303
We were only supposed
to have 45 minutes.

00:03:24.303 --> 00:03:25.338
He gave us 2 hours.

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:27.006
You know what that's like.
-Yeah.

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:28.641
So we did
a primetime special last week,

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:30.176
and you can still get it
on Paramount Plus.

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:31.610
Have you seen it yet?
-I'm very excited to see it.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:32.745
-I'm very proud of it.

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:34.613
-Oh, well,
I'm very excited to see it.

00:03:34.613 --> 00:03:36.682
I'm very excited to see
some of the items this year

00:03:36.682 --> 00:03:39.418
on this annual list.
-Me, too!

00:03:39.418 --> 00:03:41.020
-And there's one --
we talked last year.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.055
you tried to focus
on small businesses,

00:03:43.055 --> 00:03:45.891
Black-owned businesses,
women-owned businesses.

00:03:45.891 --> 00:03:47.759
-We have brand names too.

00:03:47.759 --> 00:03:49.428
-Yes, of course.
-We run the gamut.

00:03:49.428 --> 00:03:51.397
-But there was a product,
one of the products this year,

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:53.566
you had a real opportunity
to test out.

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:55.934
-I did, I did.
Because look at me, Seth.

00:03:55.934 --> 00:03:57.403
Does my skin look glowy to you?

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:59.005
-It always has.
But this year, best ever.

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:01.340
-Audience, does my skin
look glowy to you?

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.808
-Best ever.

00:04:02.808 --> 00:04:05.210
That's because I have
Dew Revive.

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:08.114
You know, my makeup artist,
Rae Dawn Brooks.

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:10.883
I'm very lucky. I have
hair and makeup every day.

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:13.986
I don't wake up this cute.
It takes a village.

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:17.924
But it's a body balm
for your face and your body,

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:19.892
whether you have eczema,
whether you have sunburn,

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:23.262
whether you just want smooth,
glowy, dewy skin, as do you.

00:04:23.262 --> 00:04:24.330
-Thank you.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.765
-As do you.
-I do want it.

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:28.200
-Okay.
-So I have this just for you.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.703
Dew Revive just for you.
-Thank you so much.

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:32.739
-You're welcome.
-Alright.

00:04:32.739 --> 00:04:35.574
-These are cool.

00:04:35.574 --> 00:04:38.644
-Phaidon Press, which does
really cool, beautiful books.

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:41.380
Tell us about these.
These are art books for kids.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:42.882
-But just open up
a couple of pages,

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:45.250
because it really
is works of art,

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:47.486
but they put it in kids' terms.
-Yes, that's very good.

00:04:47.486 --> 00:04:50.856
-So it's like, okay, rainbow
happy and sticker explosion.

00:04:50.856 --> 00:04:52.591
I know. Aw, it's so nice.

00:04:52.591 --> 00:04:54.159
I have a favorite grandson,
Luca.

00:04:54.159 --> 00:04:56.762
I'm getting him the whole thing.
He's only 2 1/2.

00:04:56.762 --> 00:04:59.064
He can't read yet, but when he
can, this is going to be good.

00:04:59.064 --> 00:05:01.900
You have
little ones at your house.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:03.069 size:63% position:69%
-I do, yeah,
and they like books.

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:05.170
-And they can read?
-They can read, yeah.

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:07.706
These are beautiful dolls.

00:05:07.706 --> 00:05:08.975
-Now I like this,

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:12.278
because this is
Alimrose Halle Ballerina dolls.

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:13.779
When Serena had her baby,
you know,

00:05:13.779 --> 00:05:16.215
she already has
an older daughter, Olympia,

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:19.084
and whenever a new baby comes,

00:05:19.084 --> 00:05:21.787
it's always good to get
the older sibling something.

00:05:21.787 --> 00:05:25.024
So I got this for Olympia,
but you can get this size,

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:27.159
and then you could get
a little baby version,

00:05:27.159 --> 00:05:28.360
so I got both of them.

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:29.594
And the beauty of this is
it comes in

00:05:29.594 --> 00:05:31.564
all different skin tones.

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:33.299
So, you know, dark skin,
light skin,

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:34.333
it's something for everybody.

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:35.701
I just think they're adorable.

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:36.601
-You know what we got my oldest
when our second was born?

00:05:36.601 --> 00:05:38.371
-What?
-A job.

00:05:38.371 --> 00:05:39.872
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:41.441
We were like,
"Free ride's over, buddy."

00:05:41.441 --> 00:05:46.812
-And what are they doing?
-They work for the city.

00:05:46.812 --> 00:05:48.047
Wait, did you have something
down there?

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:49.882
The Pride + Groom tool?

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:52.284
-Because I was thinking
about Frisbee.

00:05:52.284 --> 00:05:54.120
-Oh, is this for dogs?
-Yes.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.254
-Oh, my God.

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:57.856
-Frisbee is Seth's dog, guys.
-Yeah.

00:05:57.856 --> 00:05:59.224
-So Naomi Watts has this.

00:05:59.224 --> 00:06:01.727
it's a total grooming kit
just for your dog.

00:06:01.727 --> 00:06:03.529
So it's a --

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:05.431
-And the dog can figure out
how to use it on their own?

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:06.665
-No, no, no.
-Okay.

00:06:06.665 --> 00:06:07.900
-You know when
you're bathing Frisbee,

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.602
you can have
a latherless shampoo

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:12.137
and stuff to clip their nose,
to make their fur, you know --

00:06:12.137 --> 00:06:13.806
because those of us
who have dogs.

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:15.107
I don't have a dog
at this particular time,

00:06:15.107 --> 00:06:16.308
but I love them.

00:06:16.308 --> 00:06:18.511
But those of us
who have dogs and love dogs,

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:19.945
we treat them like children.

00:06:19.945 --> 00:06:21.714
They're just four-legged
children with fur.

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:24.016
This is what you need.
Naomi Watts does it.

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:25.451
Snoop Dog does it,
so you know it's good.

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:26.586
-Okay, that's great.

00:06:26.586 --> 00:06:27.954
-That tells you
about their client base.

00:06:27.954 --> 00:06:28.955
That's good.

00:06:28.955 --> 00:06:30.355
"Purple Rising,"
tell me about it.

00:06:30.355 --> 00:06:32.425
You have it right there
with you.

00:06:32.425 --> 00:06:36.595
-"The Color Purple."
You know, that's the movie.

00:06:36.595 --> 00:06:38.664
-That is a movie.
-It's a movie.

00:06:38.664 --> 00:06:40.098
-You had a friend in it.
-Yeah.

00:06:40.098 --> 00:06:41.701
You know, I had a friend in it.

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:44.803
Also, Seth, back in the day,

00:06:44.803 --> 00:06:46.939
I want you to know
that I was actually in it.

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:49.308
Now, if you blink,
you will miss me, but...

00:06:49.308 --> 00:06:51.110
-I didn't know this.
This is very exciting.

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:53.245
-No, if you blink,
you will miss me.

00:06:53.245 --> 00:06:55.214
But you know,
when "The Color Purple,"

00:06:55.214 --> 00:06:58.450
the book is now
over 40 years old.

00:06:58.450 --> 00:06:59.919
So they've had the book,

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:02.488
they've had a movie with Steven
Spielberg and Quincy Jones.

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:05.324
Oprah, first nominated
for an Academy Award

00:07:05.324 --> 00:07:07.126
back in the day, Whoopi.

00:07:07.126 --> 00:07:08.927
So "Color Purple"
has been around a long time.

00:07:08.927 --> 00:07:11.997
Now it's coming up and it's
going to be a new movie

00:07:11.997 --> 00:07:18.537
with Fantasia,
Taraji P. Henson, Halle Bailey.

00:07:18.537 --> 00:07:22.675
So look, "Along For the Ride."
Look, there I am.

00:07:22.675 --> 00:07:25.144
-Here, go over there.
Go over there.

00:07:25.144 --> 00:07:27.012
-Okay.
-Look at you.

00:07:27.012 --> 00:07:28.213
-I know.

00:07:28.213 --> 00:07:30.683
So I was -- This is funny.

00:07:30.683 --> 00:07:33.318
I was visiting the set one day
when Oprah was first starting,

00:07:33.318 --> 00:07:35.187
and I was so fascinated
by all things movies.

00:07:35.187 --> 00:07:36.355
And they said, "Do you want
to be in the movie?"

00:07:36.355 --> 00:07:38.024
I went, "Okay."

00:07:38.024 --> 00:07:40.125
So I was one of the extras,
but literally,

00:07:40.125 --> 00:07:42.260
you have to blink
and put it on pause to see me.

00:07:42.260 --> 00:07:43.562
But it's been around.

00:07:43.562 --> 00:07:45.497
So this is the definitive book,

00:07:45.497 --> 00:07:48.700
the behind-the-scenes stories
of how the movie was made,

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:50.603
the way the book was done,
Alice Walker.

00:07:50.603 --> 00:07:52.104
It's great
if you love "Color Purple,"

00:07:52.104 --> 00:07:53.773
and you do, audience,
and you do.

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:54.873
-And you do.

00:07:54.873 --> 00:07:56.976
You got a sweatshirt.
-Okay.

00:07:56.976 --> 00:07:59.011
This, I love.

00:07:59.011 --> 00:08:00.513
Those of us who have children --

00:08:00.513 --> 00:08:03.349
So you have "The Original."

00:08:03.349 --> 00:08:04.950
Have you guys seen this?
Okay.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:07.820
"Encore" for your child.
I like this.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:10.556
-"Remix."
-That's great.

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:11.757
-Isn't this good?
-These are very good.

00:08:11.757 --> 00:08:13.426
-I love this.

00:08:13.426 --> 00:08:16.028
-"Mic drop."

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:17.629
Very cute.

00:08:17.629 --> 00:08:18.864
This is my favorite one.

00:08:18.864 --> 00:08:21.167
"A Fresh New Beat,"
when you have the baby.

00:08:21.167 --> 00:08:23.702
-That's very nice.
-Isn't this nice?

00:08:23.702 --> 00:08:25.638
-Normally, I
bring you matching pajamas,

00:08:25.638 --> 00:08:27.139
so I tried
to change it up this year.

00:08:27.139 --> 00:08:28.640
-I'll take it.
We're very excited about that.

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:30.676
By the way, we do wear
our matching pajamas every year.

00:08:30.676 --> 00:08:33.378
And now we have these
lovely cookies.

00:08:33.378 --> 00:08:35.147
-Who doesn't like to have
matching pajamas

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:36.281
in a family photo?

00:08:36.281 --> 00:08:37.516
We have some of those, too,
on the list.

00:08:37.516 --> 00:08:40.353
-So these are
Christmas and Hanukkah cookies.

00:08:40.353 --> 00:08:41.620
-I love it.
Yeah, we got a dreidel.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:43.489
We got a Christmas tree.
These are very nice.

00:08:43.489 --> 00:08:45.857
-So we have the kit for you
that you can make it yourself.

00:08:45.857 --> 00:08:46.959
[ Laughs ]
-Mm-hmm.

00:08:46.959 --> 00:08:49.495
-You can do the icing
with the kids.

00:08:49.495 --> 00:08:53.165
-Somebody laughed like
I wasn't supposed to eat these.

00:08:53.165 --> 00:08:54.400
-Let me have one, too.
-Thank you.

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.002
And this is the whole kit
I want to show.

00:08:56.002 --> 00:08:57.703
You don't just have to work
from scratch.

00:08:57.703 --> 00:08:59.905
So this is...
-And they're soft, guys.

00:08:59.905 --> 00:09:01.140
-Alright, there you go.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.009
-So you get the icing,
you get the sprinkles.

00:09:03.009 --> 00:09:04.877
You can do it
with your favorite children.

00:09:04.877 --> 00:09:06.645
We like this, too.
-There you go.

00:09:06.645 --> 00:09:08.413
You guys this is Gayle King,
everybody!

00:09:08.413 --> 00:09:11.150
-Thank you guys!
-The cookies are delicious.

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:12.751
The full list of
Oprah's Favorite Things

00:09:12.751 --> 00:09:14.519
is available now
at OprahDaily.com,

00:09:14.519 --> 00:09:18.390
and will be featured
in the Winter 2023 issue

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:20.058
